        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Polish quota warning settings",
        "body": "## Summary\r\n- Redesign global quota warning settings into compact Session/Weekly threshold rows.\r\n- Remove the Apply button and noisy row separators.\r\n- Add `%` labels and rename threshold controls to `Warning` and `Critical`.\r\n- Dim disabled quota warning rows while preserving saved threshold values.\r\n- Save edited thresholds on Return, focus loss, outside click, or view teardown instead of requiring Apply or Return.\n- Fix the threshold field focus/loading issue by anchoring outside-click detection to the threshold editor bounds.\r\n- Ignore unchanged threshold saves to avoid unnecessary refresh churn.\r\n- Prevent provider threshold editors from re-creating stale overrides after “Customize thresholds” is disabled.\n- Preserve untouched one-value and multi-threshold lists, and keep every inherited active threshold visible.\n- Update quota warning localization copy across resource catalogs.\n\r\n## Why\r\nThe previous settings layout could wrap and misalign inside macOS SwiftUI `Form`, making the quota warning section feel buggy. Its Apply/Return-only flow also made edits easy to leave uncommitted; idempotent setters keep the broader focus-based save lifecycle from causing unnecessary refreshes.\n\r\nThe new `Warning` / `Critical` labels describe the user-facing behavior more clearly than numeric position labels: warning fires earlier, critical fires when remaining quota is low. Internally, the same threshold storage is preserved.\r\n\r\nThis makes the layout cleaner, the editing flow calmer, and the focus/save behavior more reliable.\r\n\r\n## Validation\n- focused `PreferencesPaneSmokeTests|SettingsStoreTests`: 89 tests pass\n- `make check`\n- `make test`: all 49 shards pass\n- exact-branch structured review: clean, no actionable findings\n- Developer-ID signed app on macOS 27 build 26A5368g, arm64, Xcode 26.6 / SDK 26.5\n- local-only live matrix: four minimum-size locales, focus/Tab/outside commit, Return, no-op, close/reopen, override removal, threshold-free inheritance, disabled-row dimming, and sanitization\n\r\n## Screenshot\r\n### before\r\n<img width=\"600\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-07 at 9 33 30 AM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2ebaccfb-11f2-4d58-a7fd-5b32f3575681\" />\r\n\r\n### after\r\n<img width=\"600\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-07 at 5 32 08 PM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b372810f-9e87-4c1c-84a6-9c7f006b5878\" />\r\n\r\n## Notes\r\nProvider-specific quota warning layout remains structurally unchanged apart from the shared labels and save lifecycle.\n",
